COPY public.treks (trek_id, trek_name, slug, state_id, district_id, short_description, description, difficulty, trek_type, distance_km, duration_hours, elevation_m, highest_point_m, altitude_gain_m, starting_point, ending_point, best_time, entry_fee, permit_required, is_featured, is_verified, status, created_at, updated_at, rating, duration_label, fee_basis) FROM stdin;
1	Makalidurga	makalidurga	1	10	A moderate hill-fort trek featuring rocky terrain and lake views.	Makalidurga is a hill fort near Doddaballapur. The trail climbs rocky terrain to the fort ruins and provides views of the surrounding landscape and nearby lake.	Moderate	Fort	7.00	3.00	1350	1350	350	Muthurayaswamy Temple	Makalidurga Hilltop	October - February	300.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.7	\N	\N
2	Skandagiri	skandagiri	1	5	A popular sunrise trek to an ancient hill fortress.	Skandagiri, also known as Kalavara Durga, features rocky terrain, steep climbs and the ruins of an old fort at the summit. Karnataka Eco Tourism identifies Kalwara village as the trek starting area.	Easy	Fort	8.00	2.00	1450	1450	489	Kalwara Village	Skandagiri Hilltop	August - February	250.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.8	\N	\N
3	Harihara Betta	harihara-betta	1	5	A short and scenic rocky hill trek near Bengaluru.	Harihara Betta, also called Pandava Betta or Kaurava Betta in the local area, is a compact rocky hill trek with open views and an isolated temple landscape.	Easy	Hill	6.00	2.00	1100	1100	250	Hariharapura Village	Harihara Betta Summit	October - February	0.00	f	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.6	\N	\N
4	Kudremukh	kudremukh	1	2	A scenic high-altitude trek through Kudremukh National Park.	Kudremukh is famous for its horse-face shaped peak, rolling grasslands, dense forests, streams and spectacular Western Ghats scenery. The regulated trail normally starts from the Mullodi area and requires forest permission.	Moderate	Mountain	20.00	8.00	1894	1894	1772	Mullodi	Kudremukh Peak	October - February	600.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.9	\N	\N
5	Mullayanagiri	mullayanagiri	1	2	The highest peak in Karnataka at 1930 metres.	Mullayanagiri is the highest peak in Karnataka and forms part of the Chandradrona mountain range. The summit contains a small temple and offers expansive views over the surrounding Western Ghats.	Easy	Mountain	4.00	2.00	1930	1930	400	Sarpadhari	Mullayanagiri Peak	September - February	0.00	f	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.8	\N	\N
6	Baba Budangiri	baba-budangiri	1	2	A prominent mountain range and trekking destination near Chikkamagaluru.	Baba Budangiri, also known as Dattagiri, forms part of the Chandradrona range. The area combines high-altitude landscapes, rocky trails, caves, shrines and panoramic views.	Easy	Mountain	8.00	3.00	1895	1895	347	Dattatreya Peetha	Baba Budangiri Peak	September - February	0.00	f	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.7	\N	\N
7	Netravati Peak	netr​​avati-peak	1	2	A scenic peak trek through the Kudremukh National Park landscape.	Netravati Peak offers dense forest, streams, grasslands and a final climb toward a panoramic summit. The trek is accessed from the Samse region and requires forest permission.	Moderate	Mountain	14.00	4.00	1520	1520	584	Samse	Netravati Peak	October - February	500.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.8	\N	\N
8	Ballalarayana Durga	ballalarayana-durga	1	2	A historic fort trek surrounded by Western Ghats grasslands.	Ballalarayana Durga leads through forest and open grasslands to the ruins of a historic Hoysala-era fort. The trail begins near Sunkasale and provides broad views of the surrounding mountains.	Moderate	Fort	16.00	6.00	1509	1509	517	Sunkasale	Ballalarayana Durga Fort	October - February	500.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.7	\N	\N
9	Bandaje Falls	bandaje-falls	1	4	A spectacular waterfall trek through the Charmadi Ghats.	Bandaje Falls is reached through forest and grassland terrain in the Western Ghats. The route passes near Ballalarayana Durga and descends toward the waterfall area.	Moderate	Waterfall	18.00	6.00	850	850	838	Kalabhyraveshwara Temple	Bandaje Falls	October - February	500.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.8	\N	\N
10	Ettina Bhuja	ettina-bhuja	1	4	An offbeat Charmadi Ghats peak shaped like an ox shoulder.	Ettina Bhuja, also called Shishila Gudda, is a Western Ghats peak surrounded by dense forest and grasslands. The trail is less frequented and offers panoramic views from the summit.	Moderate	Mountain	10.00	6.00	1300	1300	1079	Shishila	Ettina Bhuja Peak	October - February	500.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.7	\N	\N
11	Kumara Parvatha	kumara-parvatha	1	1	One of Karnataka's most challenging Western Ghats treks.	Kumara Parvatha, also known as Pushpagiri, rises to 1712 metres and is reached through dense forest, grasslands and exposed rocky terrain. The classic route begins at Kukke Subramanya and is generally completed over two days.	Hard	Mountain	22.00	16.00	1712	1712	1600	Kukke Subramanya	Kumara Parvatha Summit	October - February	500.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.9	\N	\N
12	Tadiandamol	tadiandamol	1	1	The highest peak in Kodagu with scenic grasslands and Shola forests.	Tadiandamol is a popular Western Ghats trek beginning near Nalaknad Palace. The trail crosses forest and open grassland before reaching the 1748 metre summit.	Moderate	Mountain	14.00	6.00	1748	1748	550	Nalaknad Palace	Tadiandamol Peak	October - February	500.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.8	\N	\N
13	Brahmagiri	brahmagiri	1	1	A forested Western Ghats peak on the Karnataka-Kerala border.	Brahmagiri rises to 1608 metres and lies within the Brahmagiri Wildlife Sanctuary. The trek passes through forested terrain and offers panoramic views from the summit.	Moderate	Mountain	8.00	6.00	1608	1608	500	Srimangala	Brahmagiri Peak	October - February	200.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.7	\N	\N
14	Nishani Motte	nishani-motte	1	1	A forest and grassland trek in the Talacauveri region.	Nishani Motte is a relatively less crowded peak in Kodagu surrounded by forest, grasslands and Western Ghats scenery. The trail is regulated and is best undertaken with a guide.	Moderate	Mountain	12.00	7.00	1276	1276	1246	Bhagamandala Forest Range	Nishani Motte Peak	October - February	350.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.8	\N	\N
15	Kote Betta	kote-betta	1	1	A scenic Kodagu peak known as Fort Hill.	Kote Betta is one of the prominent peaks around Madikeri. The trek passes through coffee plantations and forested landscapes before reaching the summit and its Shiva temple.	Moderate	Mountain	8.00	5.00	1620	1620	600	Hattihole	Kote Betta Peak	October - February	0.00	f	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.6	\N	\N
16	Antaragange	antaragange	1	9	A rocky hill and cave trek near Kolar.	Antaragange combines rocky terrain, caves and the historic Kashi Vishwanath temple complex. The trail begins near the foothill temple and climbs through boulder formations.	Easy	Cave	5.00	3.00	1226	1226	355	Jalakanteshwara Swamy Temple	Antaragange Hilltop	Year-round	250.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.6	\N	\N
17	Kunti Betta	kunti-betta	1	8	A short rocky hill trek near Pandavapura.	Kunti Betta consists of rocky hilltops surrounded by rural landscapes, paddy fields and seasonal water bodies. It is a popular short trek and sunrise destination.	Easy	Hill	5.00	3.00	878	878	152	Kachenahalli	Kunti Betta Summit	October - February	400.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.6	\N	\N
18	Savandurga	savandurga	1	6	A dramatic monolithic hill and historic fort trek near Bengaluru.	Savandurga consists of the Karigudda and Biligudda hills and is one of the largest monolithic hill formations in Asia. The trail climbs exposed rocky terrain toward the historic fort and summit area.	Moderate	Fort	6.00	3.00	1226	1226	450	Bettada Dari	Kempegowda Fort	October - February	400.00	t	f	t	active	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	2026-08-12 16:26:38.357318	4.7	\N	\N
